        "problem": "Find the point of intersection of the parabola ${y}^{2}+18x-27y+54=0$ with the $x$-axis.",
        "worked_solution": "When the parabola intersects the $x$-axis, we must have $y=0.$ So, we set $y=0$ and solve the resulting equation for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0)^{2}+18x-27(0)+54 & =0 \\\\ 18x+54 & =0 \\\\ 18x & =-54 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{54}{18} \\\\ x & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parabola intersects the $x$-axis at $(-3,0).$",
